<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  App Sandbox entitlements for the Mac App Store (MAS) build of Chip Hippo.

  A MAS build runs under Apple's App Sandbox, NOT the hardened runtime — the two
  are mutually exclusive, which is why build.mas sets hardenedRuntime:false.
  Kept to the minimum the app actually needs, because every key here is
  something a reviewer may ask about:

    * app-sandbox              required of every App Store app.
    * cs.allow-jit             V8's JIT compiler.
    * files.user-selected.*    read/write the files the user picks through the
                               native dialogs — opening and saving a project,
                               exporting/importing a desktop, loading or
                               exporting a ROM image, writing the build guide's
                               RTF, and choosing the datasheet folder. The
                               sandbox grants access only to what the user
                               selected, which is exactly how those flows work.
    * files.bookmarks.app-scope
                               THE ONE THAT IS NOT OBVIOUS. Chip Hippo re-opens
                               paths from an earlier session: the Open Recent
                               list, and the Settings ▸ Data Sheets folder read
                               when a pin-assignments window opens. A dialog's
                               grant dies with the process, so those need
                               security-scoped bookmarks (app/store/bookmark-
                               store.js) — and WITHOUT this key the dialogs hand
                               back empty bookmark strings and every one of
                               those features quietly stops working a launch
                               later.
    * network.client           the app's only outbound calls: the AI circuit
                               builder and the datasheet download. Both are
                               opt-in, and the auto-updater — the third — is
                               switched off in a store build (store-build.js).

  Deliberately ABSENT, and why:
    * network.server           nothing listens; there is no loopback server.
    * disable-library-validation
                               forbidden under the App Sandbox.
    * cs.allow-unsigned-executable-memory
                               a hardened-runtime key, meaningless here.
    * files.bookmarks.document-scope
                               that is for bookmarks stored INSIDE a document.
                               Ours live in an app-owned sidecar under
                               userData, so app-scope is the right one.
    * print, device.*, files.downloads.*
                               unused surface is unused.

  Everything the app writes for itself — the working slot, ROM .bin files,
  downloaded datasheets, settings, the encrypted API key — lives under
  userData, inside the sandbox container, and needs no entitlement at all.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
  <dict>
    <key>com.apple.security.app-sandbox</key>
    <true/>
    <key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-jit</key>
    <true/>
    <key>com.apple.security.files.user-selected.read-write</key>
    <true/>
    <key>com.apple.security.files.bookmarks.app-scope</key>
    <true/>
    <key>com.apple.security.network.client</key>
    <true/>
  </dict>
</plist>
